1. हि (cf. √ हय्) cl. 5. P. (Dhātup. xxvii, 11) हिनो॑ति (Ved. also हिनुते॑, हि॑न्वति and हिन्व॑ति, ˚ते; p. हिन्वान॑ [with act. and pass. sense] RV.; ह॑यत्, RV.; TS.; 1. sg. हिषे, RV.; pf. जिघाय, जिघ्युः, Br. &c.; जिघ्ये [with pass. sense] Bhaṭṭ.; aor. अ॑हेम, अह्यन्, हेत p. हियान॑ [with pass. sense] RV.; अह्यम् [?], अ॑हैत्, AV.; अहैषीत्, Br.; अहेषत, RV.; fut. हेता Gr.; हेष्यति, MBh. &c.; inf. -ह्ये᳙, RV.),
to send forth, set in motion, impel, urge on, hasten on (Ā. also intrans.), RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; KātyŚr.;
to stimulate or incite to (dat.), RV.;
to assist or help to (dat.), ib.;
to discharge, hurl, cast, shoot, RV.;
to convey, bring, procure, ib.; ŚBr.;
to forsake, abandon, get rid of Bhaṭṭ.;
 (हिन्वति) to gladden, delight, Dhātup. xv, 82 :
